            <ArticleTitle>Opioidphobia and cancer pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S60-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MPH.0b013e3182122059</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opioidphobia is one of the major issues in cancer pain management, opioidphobia could limit the efficacy of the treatment process. This paper shows short summary of the findings of a simple study that aimed to discuss the issue of opioidphobia in cancer pain management. Findings showed that there are two kinds; provider's obioidphobia and patient's obioidphobia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
